<title>NORWAY: Norway c.bank upgrades 1997 CPI to 2.75 pct.</title>
<headline>Norway c.bank upgrades 1997 CPI to 2.75 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norway's central bank made the following first-quarter forecasts for key economic indicator growth in percentage. The bank's fourth-quarter forecasts for 1997 made in December are included for comparison:</p>
<p>					 1997		   1998</p>
<p>						Dec</p>
<p> Private consumption     4.0	 (3.5)	    3.25</p>
<p> Public consumption	2.5	 (1.0)	    1.75</p>
<p> Total gross investment  8.5	 (2.5)	    3.75</p>
<p> Mainland demand	   4.0	 (3.25)	   3.0</p>
<p> Export			7.0	 (6.0)	    5.0</p>
<p> Import			8.25	(6.5)	    4.75</p>
<p> Overall GDP		 4.25	(3.5)	    3.25</p>
<p> Mainland GDP		3.25	(3.0)	    2.75</p>
<p> Jobless rate		4.5	 (4.0)	    4.0</p>
<p> CPI			   2.75	(2.5)	    2.0</p>
<p>Oil price per barrel</p>
<p> (crowns)		    129	 (125)	    131</p>
<p> C/A pct surplus of GDP  7.0	 (7.5)	    7.0</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
